{title: Under His Wings}
{subtitle: Psalm 91}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Eb] [Bb] | [Bb] | [Gm] [Eb] [Bb] |
| [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I have made the LORD my refuge, [Gm]the Most High my [Eb]dwelling place [Bb]
Through the snare and through the sick[Gm]ness [Eb]I am sheltered by his [Bb]grace
A [Gm]thousand fall be[F]side me [Eb]and ten thousand at my [Bb]right
[F/A]But [Gm]it will not come near me, for [Eb]I'm hidden in his [F]sight
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
He will [Bb]cover you [F]with his pin[Gm]ions
And [Eb]under his wings [Bb]you will find [F]refuge
His [Bb]faithfulness [F]is your shield [Gm]and rampart
Whoever [Eb]dwells in the [F]shelter of the Most [Gm]High
Will [Eb]rest in the [F]shadow of the Al[Bb]mighty
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I won't fear the terror of the night [Gm]or arrows [Eb]in the day [Bb]
He will command his angels [Gm]to guard me in all my [Bb]way
They [Gm]will lift me in [F]their hands [Eb]so my foot won't strike [Bb]a stone
I [Gm]will tread upon the lion and [F]the cobra, not alone
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
He [Bb]will cover [F]you with his [Gm]pinions
And [Eb]under his wings [Bb]you will find [F]refuge
His [Bb]faithfulness [F]is your shield [Gm]and rampart
Whoever [Eb]dwells in the [F]shelter of the Most [Gm]High
Will [Eb]rest in the [F]shadow of the Al[Bb]mighty
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Because [Gm]he clings to me in [Eb]love, I will rescue him
He will [Bb]call on me, and I will [F]answer him
[Gm]I will be with him in trouble
With [Eb]long life I will satisfy him
And [Bb]I will [F]show him my salvation
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Under [Bb]his wings [F]you will find [Gm]refuge
Under [Bb]his [F][Gm]wings
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Gm] | [Bb] [F] | [Gm] | [Bb] [F] |
| [Gm] | [Gm] | [Gm] |
